  "limits": [
    "User immutable is not system immutable or a multi-user authorization boundary. The private service owner can clear flags. Other protection bits including append-only remain rejected.",
    "Matches Darwin retained admission: existing writable fd descriptions and their dups keep data/size rights after the flag is set, including orphan handles. Metadata mutations remain denied. No mmap permission-revocation guarantee.",
    "New writable opens, pathname writes/truncate, mode/times/xattrs, hardlinks, unlink/rename/replacement and immutable-directory entry mutations are checked before publication. Existing mutable children of an immutable directory remain writable.",
    "Existing 72-byte FFINOD04 format is reused but the new immutable bit is rejected by older daemons. Clearing live flags does not remove reachable historical immutable records; updated daemon/module must be deployed together.",
    "Explicit administrative revision restore switches a World head and is not a POSIX data mutation to a protected inode. Native qualification covers macOS 27.2.1 arm64 private single-user disposable mount and listed operations, not full POSIX/APFS or power-loss guarantees."
  ],
